---
description: Forbid single-line function and method bodies
globs: **/*.go
alwaysApply: false
---

# No single-line functions

A function or method whose entire body is one statement adds indirection without value. Inline the call at the invocation site instead.

```go
// ❌ BAD — wrapper that just delegates
func respondNotFound(c *gin.Context) {
    c.JSON(http.StatusNotFound, gin.H{"message": "GIF not found"})
}

// ✅ GOOD — call the statement directly at the call site
c.JSON(http.StatusNotFound, gin.H{"message": "GIF not found"})
```

This applies to standalone functions, methods, and function literals alike. If the abstraction is genuinely reusable and non-trivial, give it a multi-statement body (e.g. add a log line, derive a value, or set a header before writing the response).
